\section{Control Operators and Symmetry Enforcement}

Let $(q,p)$ denote the canonical coordinates of the TSSE-governed system. Define the
control operator:
\[
\mathcal{C}(t) : (q,p) \mapsto (q,p),
\]
which applies corrective inputs to maintain TSSE invariants.

\begin{definition}[TSSE Control Operator]
A TSSE control operator $\mathcal{C}(t)$ satisfies:
\[
\mathcal{C}(t)\mathcal{U}(t) = \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{C}(t),
\]
and preserves TSSE invariants:
\[
\mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}}(\mathcal{C}(t)(q,p)) = \mathcal{I}_{\text{TSSE}}(q,p).
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Control Operator Commutation]
TSSE control operators commute with TSSE evolution.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Since $\mathcal{C}(t)$ preserves invariants and TSSE evolution preserves invariants,
their composition is commutative.
\end{proof}

This lemma establishes the algebraic consistency of TSSE control.

