\section{Hamiltonian-Consistent Control Inputs}

Let $H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}$ denote the unified engine Hamiltonian. TSSE requires that
control inputs be Hamiltonian-consistent:
\[
H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}(q,p) = H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}(\mathcal{C}(t)(q,p)).
\]

\begin{definition}[Hamiltonian-Consistent Control]
A control operator $\mathcal{C}(t)$ is Hamiltonian-consistent if:
\[
\{H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}},\mathcal{C}(t)\} = 0.
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{lemma}[Hamiltonian Preservation]
If $\mathcal{C}(t)$ is Hamiltonian-consistent, then:
\[
\frac{d}{dt}H_{\text{TSSE–AITFE}}(\mathcal{C}(t)(q,p)) = 0.
\]
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Hamiltonian invariance follows from the vanishing Poisson bracket.
\end{proof}

This lemma ensures that TSSE control does not inject or remove energy.

